{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.RothAssembly","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mathlib.RothAssembly","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.RothAlgebraicInteger","lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.RothContradiction"],"declarations":2,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.le_index_of_taylor_house","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.le_index_of_taylor_house","kind":"theorem","line":45,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RothAssembly.lean#L45-L99","doc":"**Step 2 over `𝓞 K`, assembled.**  Step 1's index at `α` (`hidx`) plus the approximation\nquality (`hγ`, `hS`) give a lower bound on the index at the rational point, with only the numeric\ncomparison `hfinal` left over.\n\n`hidx` is load-bearing: it is what restricts the sum in the `φ₀` estimate.  An earlier draft of\nthis arc considered taking the smallness directly as a hypothesis, which would have made this\nargument independent of step 1 — true, and missing the auxiliary polynomial's entire purpose. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.conjBound","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.conjBound","kind":"def","line":38,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RothAssembly.lean#L38-L43","doc":"**The bound each of the `d−1` other conjugates contributes**, already scaled by the\ndenominator `∏ q_h^{r_h}`.  Named because `eq_zero_of_norm_mul_pow_lt_one` raises it to the\n`d−1`, so slack here is `d−1` times as expensive as slack at `φ₀`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}